<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="126" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Model 1: the external-flag script treats the stamp's licensed core users (B2B guests) as internal (re-scoped 2026-10-13 under ADR-028 A9)</title>
    <phase>7 — B2B guest sign-in on Dataverse surfaces (#1453), owner 2026-10-08</phase>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Access-control flag on systemusers (security); script used by the deployment guide.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security rule change; identifies a guest's home directory without a token.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <deps>ADR-028 A9 (PR #1810); UAC-r2 answer 2026-10-13: never run -Apply on a Model 1 stamp until this task lands.</deps>
    <tags>auth, security, access-control, script, unit-test</tags>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Re-scoped on 2026-10-13 after the owner approved ADR-028 A9; see notes/126-message-to-uac-r2.md, "Update 2026-10-13 (later)". Three populations sign in to a Model 1 stamp:
- Licensed core users are B2B guests in the Spaarke tenant, with systemuser rows that carry `#EXT#`.
- Workforce contacts sign in with their company account and are not guests (A9).
- Partners are CIAM contacts.

The original goals G2 (the workforce member test for guests) and G3 (guest contact binding) are SUPERSEDED. Under A9 they are not guest paths, and SPA-r3 owns them end to end (the BFF token acceptance keyed on (tid, oid), and the stored link from a licensed user's company account to their systemuser).

What remains is G1. `scripts/Set-ExternalFlagForB2BGuests.ps1`, which the deployment guide requires, sets `sprk_isexternal = true` on every `#EXT#` systemuser. On a Model 1 stamp that is wrong: it would mark the customer's own licensed staff as external, which removes their Restricted-record shares and internal-only messages. Dev evidence: Ralph Dewey is correctly `No` today.

Step 1 DECIDED (owner 2026-10-13): option (a). A customer may license someone who is not their own staff, so the script must tell them apart. Original options, for the record:
- (a) The guest's email domain is resolved with Graph `findTenantInformationByDomainName`, and the result is in `WorkforceIdentity:CustomerTenantIds` / the provisioning customer record.
- (b) A recorded set, e.g. the stored-link (tid, oid) once SPA-r3 ships it.
- (c) Model 1 rule: every guest systemuser in the stamp is the customer's licensed staff (internal), with an explicit exception list for others.

Recommend one, with the reason; there is no home-directory claim on the systemuser (research 2026-10-12).

Step 2: implement it in the script, keeping dry run as the default. Update the deployment guide's step, and the stale D-13 comment in `WorkforceIdentityOptions.cs` (SPA-r3's file; coordinate) so it describes A8/A9.</prompt>
  <goal>On a Model 1 stamp, the external-flag script never marks the customer's licensed core users (B2B guests) as external, and still flags any guest who is not the customer's staff. The deployment guide and the D-13 comment match ADR-028 A8/A9.</goal>
  <constraints>
    <constraint>Rule is option (a), owner 2026-10-13: domain lookup via findTenantInformationByDomainName against the stamp's customer home-directory list; unresolvable = report, never flip. ADR-028 is the single authority: on a conflict, raise CLAUDE.md 6.5. Do not touch workforce-contact sign-in or the stored link (SPA-r3, A9).</constraint>
    <constraint>Do not edit UAC-r2's `tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/*` or `SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion*`; add new tests elsewhere unless UAC-r2 agrees.</constraint>
    <constraint>Any `-Apply` of the script on any environment needs the owner's go. If the rule needs BFF code, the BFF §10 obligations apply.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests for the chosen rule: on a Model 1 stamp, a guest systemuser of the customer is left internal and a guest that is not the customer's staff is flagged external. A Model 2 (customer-tenant) stamp behaves as before. Negative case: a guest whose home directory cannot be determined is reported for review, never silently flipped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On dev, the script's dry run does not list Ralph Dewey (or any customer licensed guest). The deployment guide and the D-13 comment describe A8/A9.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <justification>
    <existing>Set-ExternalFlagForB2BGuests.ps1 and sprk_isexternal eligibility (UAC-r2 task 114).</existing>
    <extension>Yes: extend the script's guest rule with the Model 1 customer case; per-stamp settings come from provisioning.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Running the guide's required script on a Model 1 stamp marks every licensed customer user external, removing their Restricted-record access and internal-only messages.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
</task>
